<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><gml:doc xmlns:gml="urn:x-gml:canonical"><gdoc sec="internal"><frontm><titlep><title>Widget Server 4.2</title>
<title>Release Notes</title>
<docnum>GC00-4200</docnum>
<date>November 6th, 2026</date>
<author>The Widget Team</author>
</titlep><abstract><p>This document describes Widget Server Version 4.2,
which runs on z/OS, z/VM, Linux on Z.
</p></abstract><toc><gml:toc-entries title="Table of Contents"><gml:toc-entry level="1" refid="over" section="body"><gml:entry-text>Overview</gml:entry-text><gml:pageref refid="over"/></gml:toc-entry><gml:toc-entry level="1" refid="changes" section="body"><gml:entry-text>Changes in 4.2</gml:entry-text><gml:pageref refid="changes"/></gml:toc-entry><gml:toc-entry level="2" refid="cfg" section="body"><gml:entry-text>Configuration</gml:entry-text><gml:pageref refid="cfg"/></gml:toc-entry><gml:toc-entry level="2" refid="cap" section="body"><gml:entry-text>Capacity planning</gml:entry-text><gml:pageref refid="cap"/></gml:toc-entry><gml:toc-entry level="2" refid="gml-h2-3" section="body"><gml:entry-text>Platforms</gml:entry-text><gml:pageref refid="gml-h2-3"/></gml:toc-entry></gml:toc-entries></toc><figlist><gml:figlist-entries title="List of Illustrations"><gml:figlist-entry refid="probs" num="1"><gml:num>Figure 1</gml:num><gml:entry-text>Problems fixed in 4.2</gml:entry-text><gml:pageref refid="probs"/></gml:figlist-entry></gml:figlist-entries></figlist></frontm><body><h1 id="over" anchor="over">Overview</h1>
<p>Widget Server 4.2 is a maintenance release.
It contains the changes listed in <hdref refid="changes" resolved="yes" target="h1">“Changes in 4.2”<gml:pageref refid="changes" when="auto" label="on page"/></hdref>.
<i1 anchor="gml-i1-1">Widget Server</i1>
<i2 anchor="gml-i2-1">version 4.2</i2>
</p><p><hp2>Internal readers:</hp2> the code freeze for
4.3 is planned for next quarter.
</p><h1 id="changes" anchor="changes">Changes in 4.2</h1>
<p>The following changes were made:
</p><ol nest="1"><li num="1"><gml:num>1.</gml:num>Faster start-up<fn id="fn1" num="1" anchor="fn1" callout="no"><gml:num>1</gml:num>Measured on a cold system.</fn>
</li><li num="2"><gml:num>2.</gml:num>New <q>quiet</q> start option
</li><li num="3"><gml:num>3.</gml:num>Fixes for the problems listed in <figref refid="probs" resolved="yes" target="fig" num="1">Figure 1<gml:pageref refid="probs" when="auto" label="on page"/></figref>
</li></ol><p>This release has 3 changes
(see footnote <fnref refid="fn1" resolved="yes" target="fn" num="1">1</fnref>).
</p><warn level="2">Important: Back up the configuration before you upgrade.
</warn><h2 id="cfg" anchor="cfg">Configuration</h2>
<p>The configuration file now accepts these keywords:
</p><dl><dt>timeout</dt>
<dd>Seconds to wait for a client (default 30).
<i1 anchor="gml-i1-2">timeout keyword</i1>
</dd><dt>quiet</dt>
<dd>Suppresses the start-up banner.
<i1 anchor="gml-i1-3">quiet keyword</i1>
</dd></dl><p>An example:
</p><xmp xml:space="preserve"><gml:scope kind="block" fill="no" align="left">  server  main
    timeout 45
    quiet
</gml:scope></xmp><fig id="probs" frame="box" num="1" anchor="probs"><ul compact="compact" nest="1"><li>WS0012: crash on empty request
</li><li>WS0019: wrong date in log
</li></ul><figcap><gml:num>Figure 1.</gml:num>Problems fixed in 4.2</figcap>
</fig><h2 id="cap" anchor="cap">Capacity planning</h2>
<p>Each worker thread of Widget Server 4.2 serves about
<m>r = 250</m> requests per second, so a server with
<m>w = 8</m> workers handles at most
<fml id="thru" num="1" anchor="thru">T = w \cdot r = 8 \cdot 250 = 2000
</fml>requests per second, or 172800000 requests a day.
</p><p>At start-up the 12 cache shards are warmed one after another,
and shard <m>k</m> takes <m>k</m> seconds, so the warm-up takes
<fml id="warm" num="2" anchor="warm">\sum_{k=1}^{12} k = {12(12+1)\over 2} = 78\ {\rm s}
</fml>before the server accepts requests.
</p><p>Plan the offered load <m>\lambda</m> so that the utilisation
<m>\rho</m> stays at or below 0.8.
With <m>\lambda = 1600</m> requests per second and <m>T</m> from
<fmlref refid="thru" resolved="yes" target="fml" num="1">(1)</fmlref>,
<fml id="util" num="3" anchor="util">\rho = {\lambda \over T} = {1600 \over 2000} = 0.80 \le 0.8
</fml>If <m>\rho</m> in <fmlref refid="util" resolved="yes" target="fml" num="3">(3)</fmlref> rises above the limit, add workers:
by <fmlref refid="thru" resolved="yes" target="fml" num="1">(1)</fmlref> each one adds 250 requests per second.
</p><h2 anchor="gml-h2-3">Platforms</h2>
<p>Supported platforms:
</p><sl><li>z/OS
</li><li>z/VM
</li><li>Linux on Z
</li></sl><warn>Note: All platforms need the latest service level.
</warn></body><backm><index><gml:index-entries title="Index"><gml:index-group letter="Q"><gml:index-entry level="1"><gml:index-term>quiet keyword</gml:index-term><gml:pageref refid="gml-i1-3"/></gml:index-entry></gml:index-group><gml:index-group letter="T"><gml:index-entry level="1"><gml:index-term>timeout keyword</gml:index-term><gml:pageref refid="gml-i1-2"/></gml:index-entry></gml:index-group><gml:index-group letter="W"><gml:index-entry level="1"><gml:index-term>Widget Server</gml:index-term><gml:pageref refid="gml-i1-1"/><gml:index-entry level="2"><gml:index-term>version 4.2</gml:index-term><gml:pageref refid="gml-i2-1"/></gml:index-entry></gml:index-entry></gml:index-group></gml:index-entries></index></backm></gdoc></gml:doc>